{{also|säugen}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈzaʊ̯ɡn̩]|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|sūgan||to suck|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*sūganą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*sug-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*suk-}}. Compare Low German {{term|sugen|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|zuigen|lang=nl}}, Danish {{term|suge|lang=da}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|saugt|sog|gesogen|past subjunctive=söge}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=de}} to [[suck]]; to create underpressure with a tube-like object such as one's mouth
#: '''''saugen''' an etwas'' — “to suck on something”
# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} to [[suck]] (something)
# {{context|colloquial|transitive|lang=de}} to [[download]] something

